From 18f3bdc23de22e57647440ffb94c0b446c978d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:39:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UI: FSR 1 without the AMD SDK, NVIDIA Image Scaling upscaler

The spatial FidelityFX effects (FSR 1 EASU and RCAS, CAS) are built-in
shaders that don't need the FidelityFX SDK, but were only compiled in
when it was found. They're now always built; the temporal FSR 2/3 path
still needs the SDK.

Adds NVIDIA Image Scaling (present_effect nis, D3D12 only, FSR on
Vulkan; present_nis_sharpness, default 0.5) from the NVIDIA Image
Scaling SDK v1.0.3 (MIT, thirdparty/nis). NVScaler upscales by 1x to 2x
along each axis, so it's chained like the EASU passes for bigger
factors, sharpening only in the last pass; without upscaling, NVSharpen.
Both are compute shaders (guest_output_nis.cs.hlsl, with the filter
banks as constant arrays instead of textures) writing to an
intermediate image as a UAV, followed by a bilinear pass to the back
buffer.

Also sizes the RTV heap for every intermediate image: it had room for
kGuestOutputMailboxSize - 1 (2), so a chain needing 3 (FSR from 720p to
8K) wrote past it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
